WEBVTT

1-1
00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:04.210 line:88% size:86% align:center
A demonstration shows how a task should unfold. A short instruction may

1-2
00:00:04.210 --> 00:00:08.321 line:88% size:86% align:center
leave the layout, the grasp, and the order of operations underspecified.

2-1
00:00:11.100 --> 00:00:14.391 line:88% size:86% align:center
Text plans and predicted futures are useful forms of

2-2
00:00:14.391 --> 00:00:17.682 line:88% size:86% align:center
guidance. But generating futures can add cost, and a

2-3
00:00:17.682 --> 00:00:20.973 line:88% size:86% align:center
static reference cannot reveal what the robot actually completed.

3-1
00:00:23.100 --> 00:00:28.464 line:88% size:86% align:center
RoboDemo accepts human demonstrations, or retrieves compatible robot videos from its training

3-2
00:00:28.464 --> 00:00:33.828 line:88% size:86% align:center
bank. Retrieval uses the initial scene and instruction, never future query frames.

4-1
00:00:34.200 --> 00:00:38.911 line:88% size:86% align:center
Sparse semantic frames and dense motion clips are encoded together. Each chronological segment

4-2
00:00:38.911 --> 00:00:43.622 line:88% size:86% align:center
writes a small fast-weight memory. This is not fine-tuning the whole policy.

5-1
00:00:44.200 --> 00:00:49.813 line:88% size:86% align:center
Demonstration memory stays protected. Separate progress memory receives the new observation, robot

5-2
00:00:49.813 --> 00:00:55.426 line:88% size:86% align:center
state, and preceding executed action, only after each real transition completes.

6-1
00:00:56.200 --> 00:01:00.961 line:88% size:86% align:center
Each action block reads intent, then progress refines the action representation,

6-2
00:01:00.961 --> 00:01:05.722 line:88% size:86% align:center
without rewriting reference memory. During denoising, both memories are read only.

7-1
00:01:06.200 --> 00:01:10.485 line:88% size:86% align:center
These are real references and recorded simulated executions, not generated

7-2
00:01:10.485 --> 00:01:14.771 line:88% size:86% align:center
robot footage. The website preserves counterexamples and failed endings.

8-1
00:01:15.200 --> 00:01:19.138 line:88% size:86% align:center
With human references, RoboDemo reaches eighty four point six

8-2
00:01:19.138 --> 00:01:23.076 line:88% size:86% align:center
percent first success on Full Fifty: sixteen hundred ninety

8-3
00:01:23.076 --> 00:01:27.014 line:88% size:86% align:center
two of two thousand trials. Retrieved-reference control remains unreported.
